The Undermountain is a great dungeon of many levels beneath the city of Waterdeep on [[Geography/Ushas/index|Ushas]]. Each floor is a wholly different region, and time runs slower the deeper one goes. Its architect built it and lives at its bottom, the twenty-fourth level.

The sixth floor is the Archive: an endless and exceptionally dangerous repository of all the knowledge on Ushas. It can be summoned from anywhere on Ushas wherever enough books are gathered in one place. The Archive is a [[Geography/Althane/The Archive|Thessian]], and in its own way it aided those who came to it with knowledge.

The eleventh floor is a giant tower built around an hourglass mounted on a pin of [[Phenomena/Holy Gold|holy gold]]. A dragon guarded it. That pin is a godslaying needle, and the only one truly from Ushas's sphere.

On the twenty-fourth level wait Control, the architect's tiefling son (his name is a virtue name; he is no Thessian), and Monday, a guardian of the Undermountain. Past them sits the architect himself.

The party that would found [[Org/Sedecium|Sedecium]] ([[People/Dorcan|Dorcan]], [[People/Zugg|Zugg]], [[People/Rotok|Rotok]] and [[People/Althane/The Broker|T3C]]) went into the Undermountain to train, and made their fortune in its first half. On the eleventh floor they solved the hourglass's puzzle by turning time back around the guardian dragon until it was a hatchling, and took the needle. Years later the [[Divinity/The Narrative/Menhir|Menhir]] showed them a second way in, to the twenty-fourth level. They defeated Control and Monday, and the architect gave his life to make a [[Phenomena/Locus|Locus]] that sent them to the [[Geography/Ushas/Far Realms|Far Realms of Ushas]], where [[Divinity/Unknown Entities/Mephistopheles|Mephistopheles]] sat.
